{"name":"Don’t Be Shy","hex":"#ed2c1a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"don’t","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Do not (negative auxiliary).","Does not."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Stop!"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/don%E2%80%99t"},{"term":"shy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Tachawit. The native name for the Shawiya language."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily frightened; timid.","Reserved; disinclined to familiar approach."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shyness","blocks":[{"text":"Shyness is a psychological trait characterized by social inhibition and apprehension in response to new social environments or perceived social judgement. It is frequently associated with social avoidance. Although shyness can be an attribute of people who have low self-esteem, the trait is often defined by a concern regarding the negative evaluation of others, such as mocking or rejection. While shyness is considered a normal personality variant, it is distinct from clinical conditions such as social anxiety disorder, which involves impairment in daily functioning."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/20220801_Introversion_-_Shyness_-_Social_anxiety_disorder_-_comparative_chart.svg/330px-20220801_Introversion_-_Shyness_-_Social_anxiety_disorder_-_comparative_chart.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shyness"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Group_of_children_in_a_village_in_West_Bengal%2C_Purba_Bardhaman.jpg/500px-Group_of_children_in_a_village_in_West_Bengal%2C_Purba_Bardhaman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Group_of_children_in_a_village_in_West_Bengal%2C_Purba_Bardhaman.jpg/1280px-Group_of_children_in_a_village_in_West_Bengal%2C_Purba_Bardhaman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Group_of_children_in_a_village_in_West_Bengal%2C_Purba_Bardhaman.jpg/500px-Group_of_children_in_a_village_in_West_Bengal%2C_Purba_Bardhaman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Putting one's hand over their mouth while laughing is often seen as an example of shyness in certain cultures (first child), as is hiding behind somebody else's back (third child)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGroup_of_children_in_a_village_in_West_Bengal%2C_Purba_Bardhaman.jpg"}],"sounds":{"don’t":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ee/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-don%27t.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/ee/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-don%27t.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-don%27t.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/ee/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-don%27t.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-don%27t.wav.ogg"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/87/En-us-don%27t.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/87/En-us-don%27t.ogg/En-us-don%27t.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fa/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-don%27t2.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/fa/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-don%27t2.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhu